      "raw_response": "Claim: Propriospinal interneurons that play a role in the plastic reorganization of spinal circuits are integral for recovery from spinal cord injury.\n\nANSWER: SUPPORTED. The abstract directly supports the claim, citing a study which demonstrates that propriospinal relay connections can mediate spontaneous functional recovery after severe SCI, even with total interruption of long descending pathways, suggesting that reorganization of these connections is crucial for recovery. (Source: [Kiefer et al., 2017](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/28683784)\n\nThe confidence level is high due to direct evidence from the study mentioned in the abstract.",
